  "body": "## What changed\n\nSeven new OpenAI-compatible providers, ported from upstream with our fork's conventions.\n\n| Provider | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `qwencloud` | QwenCloud Token Plan | OpenAI-compatible, `REASONING_CONTENT` replay |\n| `qwencloud_coding` | QwenCloud Coding Plan | same family, coding-plan endpoint |\n| `agnes` | Agnes AI gateway | `ChatTemplateReasoning(enable_thinking)` |\n| `wandb` | W&B Inference | `ChatTemplateReasoning`, `max_completion_tokens` |\n| `bedrock` | Amazon Bedrock Mantle | bearer-token OpenAI-compatible, **no AWS SigV4** |\n| `tokenrouter` | TokenRouter gateway | OpenAI-compatible, configurable base URL |\n| `nararoute` | NaraRoute gateway | OpenAI-compatible, configurable base URL |\n\nEach follows the standard provider pattern: catalog descriptor + base-URL constant, settings fields (api-key/base-url/proxy), OpenAI-chat profile, provider-manifest override, smoke field, `.env.example`, catalog-order test, runtime-instantiation test, and a focused provider test.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full suite: **3907 passed / 6 failed** — the 6 are the pre-existing PowerShell-installer checksum failures (baseline unchanged).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: all clean.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Our fork uses plain `str` settings fields (`default=\"\"`) and a manual smoke-field + `.env.example` list, not upstream's annotated types / auto-generated lists — matched ours exactly.\n- The provider-runtime builtin test now seeds the seven new API keys.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `bedrock`, `tokenrouter`, `nararoute` ship a default base URL; regional/compute-specific deployments need the corresponding `*_BASE_URL` override (documented in `.env.example`).\n- No live chat round-trip has been made against any of the seven (no keys available) — model listing and request-body construction are tested; the first user with a key is the real smoke test.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
