    "message": "feat(providers): add qwencloud, qwencloud_coding, agnes, wandb, bedrock, tokenrouter, nararoute\n\nSeven new OpenAI-compatible providers, ported from upstream with our fork's catalog\ngrouping, manual smoke-field and env-list conventions.\n\n- qwencloud (Token Plan), qwencloud_coding (Coding Plan) — QwenCloud OpenAI-compatible\n- agnes (Agnes AI), wandb (W&B Inference) — ChatTemplateReasoning(enable_thinking)\n- bedrock (Amazon Bedrock Mantle) — bearer-token OpenAI-compatible, NO AWS SigV4\n- tokenrouter, nararoute — OpenAI-compatible gateways\n\nStandard 10-file provider pattern per provider: catalog descriptor + base-URL constant,\nsettings api-key/base-url/proxy fields, OpenAI-chat profile, provider-manifest override,\nsmoke field, .env.example, catalog-order test, provider runtime instantiation test, and\na focused provider test.\n\nVerification: full suite 3907 passed / 6 pre-existing PS-installer failures (baseline\nunchanged); ruff format/check + ty clean. The provider-runtime builtin test now seeds the\nseven new keys; the new provider tests use the MessagesRequest.model_validate pattern\n(system prompt is not auto-injected), matching test_zai.py.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
